summary: Regression test
description: |
    Directly use ``vmalloc()`` from kernel module. Allocate at __init and
    free at __exit.


    Parameter(of the module):
    vm_buf_size:
            The number of pages to be allocated by vmalloc(), can be used
            in runtest.sh like ``insmod vmalloc.ko vm_buf_size=256``. On a
            system of 4kB pagesize, this will allocate 1mB non-contiguous
            memory.
contact: Shizhao Chen <shichen@redhat.com>
id: e9e505ad-b4c6-47bb-ac55-53c9b3bba9b4
test: bash ./runtest.sh
framework: beakerlib
path: /general/memory/function/noncontiguous_vmalloc
require:
  - make
  - yum-utils
recommend:
  - '@development'
duration: 1h
extra-summary: kernel vmalloc sanity test
extra-task: kernel vmalloc sanity test
